//! `cargo xtask riscos-vectors <dir> [--write-sample]`: the RISC OS
//! emulator's ARM conformance vectors (`plans/RISCOS-EMULATOR.md` §2.6).
//!
//! The source is the `SingleStepTests` ARM7TDMI suite (MIT), generated by the
//! `NanoBoyAdvance` emulator rather than captured from silicon. The ARM7TDMI is
//! an ARMv4T core. Its ARM-state files are replayed on the 26-bit profile, an
//! ARMv4 one; its Thumb files and `BX` on the 32-bit profile, an ARMv7 one,
//! which defines what ARMv4T does wherever ARMv4T defines it. A vector is
//! dropped where its result the older architecture leaves open or the profile
//! chooses differently (see [`Dropped`]); the multiplies' carry and overflow,
//! which ARMv4 leaves UNPREDICTABLE, are not compared. A failure names the
//! file, the vector and the instruction.
//!
//! `--write-sample` also writes the samples the crate's tests replay in `ci`,
//! one per profile, with the suite's licence and a provenance record.
//! Developer-run only: `<dir>` holds the suite at [`COMMIT`], its
//! `v1/*.json.bin` and its `LICENSE`, each refused unless it hashes to its
//! pin.

